results.translation:
Proverbs.

... whoever is wise listens to counsels. A fool immediately shows his anger; but he who dissembles injury is shrewd. He who speaks what he knows is a judge of justice; but he who lies is a deceitful witness. There is one who promises rashly and is pierced by the sword of conscience; but the tongue of the wise is health. The lip of truth shall be firm forever; but he who is a hasty witness fashions a tongue of lies. Deceit is in the heart of those who plot evil; but joy follows those who take counsels of peace. Whatever happens to the just man will not grieve him; but the wicked shall be filled with evil. Lying lips are an abomination to the Lord; but those who act faithfully please him. A crafty man conceals knowledge, and the heart of fools proclaims folly. The hand of the strong shall rule; but the slack hand shall serve under tribute. Grief in the heart of a man humbles him; but with a good word he shall be gladdened. He who neglects loss for the sake of a friend is just; but the way of the wicked shall deceive them. The deceitful man shall not find gain; and the substance of man shall be the price of gold. In the path of justice is life; but the deviant way leads to death. Chapter 13.

A wise son [heeds] the doctrine of his father; but he who is a scoffer does not listen when he is rebuked. From the fruit of his mouth a man shall be filled with good things; but the soul of the wicked [feeds on] iniquity. He who guards his mouth guards his soul; but he who is reckless in speaking shall meet with evils. The sluggard desires and desires not; but the soul of those who labor shall be enriched. The just man will detest a lying word; but the wicked confounds and shall be confounded. Justice guards the way of the innocent; but wickedness overthrows the sinner. There is one who is as if rich though he has nothing; and one who is as if poor though he has many riches. The ransom of a man's soul is his riches;

but the poor man endures no rebuke. The light of the just rejoices; but the lamp of the wicked shall be extinguished. Among the proud there is always strife; but those who do all things with counsel are ruled by wisdom. Substance hastily gained shall be diminished; but that which is gathered little by little by hand shall be multiplied. Hope deferred afflicts the soul; a tree of life is a desire fulfilled. He who detracts from anything binds himself for the future; but he who fears the commandment shall dwell in peace. Deceitful souls wander in sins; but the just are merciful and show mercy. Nor is there a fountain of life for the wise man, that he might turn aside from the ruin of death. Good doctrine gives grace; but in the path of scorners is an abyss. The shrewd man does all things with counsel; but the fool displays folly. A wicked messenger falls into evil; but a faithful ambassador brings health. Poverty and disgrace come to him who forsakes discipline; but he who submits to correction shall be glorified. A desire, when fulfilled, delights the soul; fools detest those who flee evils. He who walks with the wise shall be wise; the friend of fools shall become like them. Evil pursues sinners; but good things shall be repaid to the just. A good man leaves heirs, children and grandchildren; and the substance of the sinner is kept for the just. Much food is in the fallow fields of the fathers; and for others it is gathered without judgment. He who spares the rod hates his son; but he who loves him corrects him diligently. The just man eats and fills his soul; but the belly of the wicked is never satisfied. Chapter 14.

A wise woman builds her house; the foolish woman shall tear down with her own hands what she has built. He who walks in a straight path and fears God is despised by him who walks in a way of shame [pride]. In the mouth of a fool is a rod of pride; the lips of the wise preserve them. Where there are no oxen, the manger is empty;

